    "physical_description": null,
    "summary": "A Micmac birchbark container (mocock) with etched linear design, wide and rectangular at the base with a smaller, circular opening at the top. The sides are joined by inverted Y seams stitched with plant fibre cord (spruce root?), that is also wrapped around the rim of the opening. There was likely once a plant fibre strap, although now there are only fragments of such a strap at opposite sides of the top opening. There is extensive discolouring inside the box, indicating historic use (maple syrup?). The base of the box has a number of small cracks and one significant break running from front to back.",
